From 2b11b79ed65e362c21a381cb1f7b57954f442b67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:12:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] soc: apple: sep-a9: passive endpoint discovery and
 corrected transfers

The first sepOS boot (2026-10-26, pongoOS cold path) showed how sepOS
announces its services on endpoint 0xfd: op 0 with param = endpoint ID
and its 4CC in data (most significant byte first), then op 1 with the
OOL page-count ranges, data bytes LSB first = in min, in max, out min,
out max in 4 KiB pages (AppleSEPDiscovery, "OOL in [%u,%u] OOL out
[%u,%u]"):

  ep=fd op=00 param=00 data=636e746c   cntl
  ep=fd op=01 param=00 data=00000000   no OOL
  ep=fd op=00 param=10 data=78617273   xars
  ep=fd op=01 param=10 data=08080808   32 KiB in and out
  ep=fd op=00 param=13 data=7861726d   xarm

Rework the driver to match (docs/sep/linux-bringup-next.md section 2):

- endpoint table for the whole 8-bit namespace (was 16 entries; 0x10
  and 0x13 were rejected), filled passively from op 0/op 1 pairs. An
  endpoint is usable only when both halves are known. debugfs
  "endpoints" lists name, ID, source and page ranges; "log" annotates
  the 0xfd lines.
- "advertise" declares an advertisement by hand from a pongoOS capture
  (fields or the two raw data words). It only fills the table and can't
  override a value the mailbox delivered.
- "ool" takes "EP SEND RECV": separate sizes, 4 KiB multiples inside
  the advertised ranges ("in" = send). Both buffers are zeroed,
  cleaned+invalidated, published through cntl (0x04/0x02/0x05/0x03) and
  never freed once any control message went out.
- every write waits for room in the AP->SEP FIFO (snd_sts bit 16, as in
  all Apple mailbox variants) and is refused before the mailbox is armed.
- a transfer completes only on its endpoint plus tag and command; a tag
  0xff reply decodes the status word at receive OOL offset 0x10, and the
  0xfd/0xfe chunk tags fail the transfer instead of passing for
  completion.
- the completion data field is the payload length; the 7-byte header is
  not part of it (the old code turned the 32-byte 0x2b reply into 25
  bytes). Invalidate [recv, recv + 7 + len) before copying.
- "sbio" accepts only an endpoint whose complete advertisement names it
  'sbio'; a successful debugfs 0x73 on it marks SBIO ready.
- /dev/sep-bio never sends: enrol/verify return -ENOSYS until the real
  EnrollMode/MatchMode payloads exist. The zero-payload path, the
  bio_payload override and the sbio_ep module parameter are gone.

Nothing is sent automatically: arming, publishing and every command are
explicit debugfs writes. Multi-chunk transfers and IRQs are still not
implemented.
